  "digest": "# ENERGY \u2014 sector digest, ISO week 2026-W45\n\n**Coverage changes.** Five initiations published: coal-logistics TCPI (SELL, Rp1,196), RIGS (BUY, Rp1,462), RMKE (SELL, Rp151), TEBE (HOLD, Rp1,475), and oil-and-gas downstream RAJA (HOLD, Rp390). Six updates: PTBA held BUY at Rp4,947 after the QC revision removed a double-deducted FY2025 dividend; BSSR HOLD Rp4,877 on the 4 November peer re-mark; ITMG HOLD Rp20,417, FY2026E re-based to the six-month run-rate with an onerous Indominco renewal charged; IATA moved REDUCE to BUY at Rp93 as a fuel double-count left the cost line; PSSI moved to SELL Rp244 after the 1:30 bonus; CBRE SELL, equity worth about Rp2 per post-rights share. Twenty-eight names are now published across COAL, COAL_LOGISTICS and OIL_GAS_DOWNSTREAM \u2014 9 BUY, 7 HOLD, 9 SELL, 2 REDUCE, 1 NOT RATED [coverage state; ticker reports].\n\n**Deck moves.** No variable was re-reviewed this week (last review 26 October); the marks moved instead. Newcastle spot US$150.35 sits 27% above FY2027E 118.0 and ICI-4 US$65.06 24% above 52.5 [coal deck S19/S47] \u2014 the war-premium carry the desk does not expect to persist. Oil's spot mark is US$97.1 Brent and US$90.34 WTI (6 November) against 84.0 and 78.0 paths, a gap near 16%, about half last week's as the Hormuz bid unwound [oil deck].\n\n**Material news.** DSI's mechanism was clarified: sole intermediary for coal, CPO and ferro-alloy exports from 1 January 2027, taking no ownership of the goods, setting its own export reference price; its fee still awaits Danantara and BP BUMN approval [triage 3-6 November]. Two tankers burned in the Strait of Hormuz on 6 November; Brent fell 8% on 5 November on US election and ceasefire hopes, then rebounded US$3 [triage 5-6 November]. ITMG's Rp2.31trn buyback began 5 November [triage 5 November]. Early-November HBA slipped while low-calorie grades rose [triage 4 November].\n\n**What to watch.** The DSI fee, and whether it lands as a cost or a price effect before go-live; BYAN's 23 November EGMS; PTBA's 2027 RKAB and the April 2027 Banko Barat permit; and twelve sign-offs still parked, which leaves oil-and-gas upstream (ENRG, RATU) unpublished.\n\n*Research only; not a recommendation to act.*",
  "digest_file": "fund record"
